From: FreeCIE <freecie@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:57:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Take the PIN as bytes and record the VERIFY status

startSecureChannel/verifyPin took the PIN as a String, which cannot be
erased. Take the ASCII digits as a ByteArray the caller wipes, and send it
without making a String copy.

Keep the status word of the last VERIFY PIN in CieCommands.lastPinStatus:
verifyPin maps every unknown status to 0 ("blocked"), and the app needs
the real status to tell a blocked PIN from an unexpected card answer.
---
 .../it/pagopa/io/app/cie/cie/commands/CieCommands.kt     | 6 +++++-
 .../java/it/pagopa/io/app/cie/cie/commands/IasUtils.kt   | 9 ++++++---
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CieSDK/src/main/java/it/pagopa/io/app/cie/cie/commands/CieCommands.kt b/CieSDK/src/main/java/it/pagopa/io/app/cie/cie/commands/CieCommands.kt
index 482c474..73529a7 100644
